  "obligation": "Shared-VM table imports and re-exports preserve original resource/capture identity, limit contracts, typed linking errors and observable initialization trap effects.",
  "representation": "WasmTableInitializer is Reference(WasmReferenceInitializer) or Import(WasmImportName). Table declarations alone own import names/order and expected type/limits; table_imports derives the host projection. Runtime consumes rooted handles, validates external kind, exact reference type and limits against current cell size/original maximum, then inserts the same Value in the captured instance bindings. Re-export projects that Value. No copied table, extra owner map, import opcode or executor. Existing function cells/canonical signature pools retain cross-program captures. Typed WasmLink error payload is separate from traps and unsupported residuals.",
